        <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 2, 2026</p>
        <p>Professor Jerry RV is built around practical education and clear explanations. When we discuss products,
          services, or business partners, we want visitors to understand whether a commercial relationship is involved.
        </p>
        <h2>Sponsored content and paid placements</h2>
        <p>Some website areas may feature paid advertisements, sponsored listings, or partner promotions. When a
          placement is paid or sponsored, we intend to identify it clearly using language such as
          <strong>Sponsored</strong> or <strong>Advertisement</strong>.</p>
        <h2>Affiliate links and referral compensation</h2>
        <p>Some links may be affiliate or referral links. If a visitor purchases through such a link, Professor Jerry RV
          may receive compensation at no additional cost to the visitor. We will identify material affiliate or referral
          relationships where they are relevant to a recommendation.</p>
        <h2>Product recommendations</h2>
        <p>Our goal is to recommend products and services based on usefulness, suitability, and real-world RV
          considerations-not simply compensation. A product mention is not a guarantee of performance, availability,
          compatibility, or suitability for every RV.</p>
        <h2>Atlas RV Solutions</h2>
        <p><a href="https://AtlasRV.solutions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atlas RV Solutions</a> is a
          related Professor Jerry project developing RV storage and organization products. References to Atlas products
          are not independent third-party endorsements; this relationship is disclosed so visitors can evaluate those
          recommendations in context.</p>
        <h2>Independent inspections</h2>
        <p>Advertising and referral relationships should not determine the findings of an RV inspection. Inspection
          observations and reports are intended to reflect the condition and limitations of the RV examined, rather than
          the interests of advertisers or sellers. Any actual or potential conflict of interest should be disclosed
          before accepting an engagement.</p>
        <h2>Third-party claims</h2>
        <p>Third-party advertisers and merchants are responsible for their own product descriptions, warranties,
          pricing, and claims. Visitors should verify important details directly with the provider.</p>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For questions about a featured product, an advertising relationship, or this disclosure, email <a
            href="mailto:info@ProfessorJerryRV.com">info@ProfessorJerryRV.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
